1
00:00:00,900 --> 00:00:06,922
今天给大家介绍我在 2022 年做的一项独立研究：一种用计算机生成住宅平面的方法。
Today I'd like to introduce an independent study I did in 2022: a way of generating apartment floor plans by computer.

2
00:00:07,372 --> 00:00:11,865
核心算法，叫做波函数坍缩，英文缩写是 WFC。
The core algorithm is called wave function collapse — WFC for short.

3
00:00:14,365 --> 00:00:21,262
这种算法，由马克西姆·古敏提出。它只依靠两样东西：随机，和相邻单元之间的局部约束。
The algorithm was proposed by Maxim Gumin. It relies on only two things: randomness, and local constraints between neighbouring cells.

4
00:00:21,712 --> 00:00:25,108
所以它不依赖已有的经验，可以产生全新的设计。
So it does not depend on past experience, and can produce entirely new designs.

5
00:00:25,558 --> 00:00:30,786
从最基本的家具和人体工程的逻辑出发，自下而上，生成整个平面。
Starting from the basic logic of furniture and ergonomics, it generates the whole plan from the bottom up.

6
00:00:32,686 --> 00:00:37,263
波函数坍缩算法，不善于解决大、而且特定性强的网格。
Wave function collapse is not good at large grids with highly specific requirements.

7
00:00:37,263 --> 00:00:40,742
在我们的场合下，效率和细节，不可兼得。
In our case, efficiency and detail cannot both be had.

8
00:00:41,192 --> 00:00:43,537
网格选择在此，是相当关键的问题。
So the choice of grid is a crucial question here.

9
00:00:43,537 --> 00:00:48,522
我没有用常见的 20 厘米或 30 厘米网格，而是选了 55 厘米。
Instead of the usual 20 or 30 cm grid, I chose 55 cm.

10
00:00:48,972 --> 00:00:55,934
这是一个人站立时包含两臂的宽度，也接近衣柜的进深、最窄的过道，以及橱柜台面的深度。
That is the width of a standing person including both arms — and close to the depth of a wardrobe, the narrowest passage, and the depth of a kitchen counter.

11
00:00:56,384 --> 00:01:03,069
在这种网格下，墙的厚度四舍五入算作零个格子；而门，四舍五入变成两格宽。
On this grid, wall thickness rounds to zero cells, and a door rounds to two cells wide.

12
00:01:04,969 --> 00:01:07,962
我采用的方法，先要把平面图变成像素。
The method I use first turns the plan into pixels.

13
00:01:08,412 --> 00:01:15,546
床、衣柜、过道、门、窗，每个格子得到一个编码，也就是一种颜色。
Bed, wardrobe, passage, door, window: every cell gets a code, which is to say a colour.

14
00:01:15,996 --> 00:01:21,309
任意相邻的四个格子，组成一块拼图：四个角，各带一种颜色。
Any four neighbouring cells form one tile: four corners, each carrying a colour.

15
00:01:23,209 --> 00:01:26,775
连接的可能性非常多，手工定义很容易出错。
The possible connections are vast, and defining them by hand is easily buggy.

16
00:01:27,224 --> 00:01:32,898
所以，连接库是从样本里自动提取的。这可以看作一种机器学习。
So the library of connections is extracted automatically from samples. It can be seen as a kind of machine learning.

17
00:01:32,898 --> 00:01:36,811
不过，样本库的完善度，会对生成产生局限。
However, how complete the sample library is limits what can be generated.

18
00:01:37,261 --> 00:01:43,239
19 个卧室样本，给出 179 种拼接，以及每一种出现的频率。
Nineteen bedroom samples yield 179 connections, and how often each one occurs.

19
00:01:45,739 --> 00:01:50,319
一个房间的生成，从一扇门开始，因为一个房间总会有入口。
Generating a room starts from a door, because a room always has an entrance.

20
00:01:50,319 --> 00:01:53,033
在这个确定的位置上，就首先坍缩。
That position is certain, so it collapses first.

21
00:01:53,483 --> 00:01:58,658
其他的位置，还处于“叠加态”，但是我们可以计算它们的熵。
The other positions are still in superposition, but we can compute their entropy.

22
00:01:58,658 --> 00:02:04,018
这里的熵，是一个信息论的概念：可能性越集中的位置，熵越低。
Entropy here is a concept from information theory: the more concentrated the possibilities at a position, the lower its entropy.

23
00:02:04,468 --> 00:02:10,779
每一步，计算所有待定位置的熵，让熵最低的那一个，坍缩成一块合法的拼图。
At each step the entropy of every open position is computed, and the one with the lowest entropy collapses into a valid tile.

24
00:02:10,779 --> 00:02:15,467
如果有若干位置的熵相等，就让其中一个随机的位置坍缩。
If several positions tie, one of them is chosen at random.

25
00:02:15,917 --> 00:02:18,914
走进无解的死路，就推倒再来。
A dead end with no solution means starting over.

26
00:02:19,364 --> 00:02:23,976
绝大多数尝试会失败。只有较小的几率，一个房间闭合了。
Most attempts fail. Only with a small probability does a room close.

27
00:02:29,476 --> 00:02:34,241
闭合的房间，接着要打分。评分是几个方面的加权。
A closed room is then scored. The score is a weighted sum of several aspects.

28
00:02:34,691 --> 00:02:37,710
其一，周长与面积之比，越小越好。
First, the ratio of perimeter to area: the smaller the better.

29
00:02:37,710 --> 00:02:41,673
这引导房间尽量方正，但是这不是唯一的标准。
This steers a room towards a compact, square shape — but it is not the only criterion.

30
00:02:42,123 --> 00:02:48,108
其二，面积合理。面积的分数先升后降：超过合适的大小，分数就回落。
Second, a reasonable area. The area score rises, then falls: past a suitable size it drops again.

31
00:02:48,108 --> 00:02:51,662
高档住宅的空间比较宽松，回落得慢一些。
Upscale housing is more generous with space, so its score drops more slowly.

32
00:02:52,112 --> 00:02:56,389
其三，储物空间，这是越多越好，但边际收益递减。
Third, storage: the more the better, with diminishing returns.

33
00:03:00,489 --> 00:03:05,387
卧室、卫生间、厨房、客厅，各自生成，各自评分。
Bedroom, bathroom, kitchen, living room: each is generated and scored on its own.

34
00:03:05,387 --> 00:03:07,942
客厅会是整个户型的枢纽。
The living room becomes the hub of the whole apartment.

35
00:03:08,392 --> 00:03:14,138
高分的房间被留下，接到客厅预留的开口上，拼成一套完整的住宅。
The high-scoring rooms are kept and attached to the openings reserved in the living room, forming a complete apartment.

36
00:03:14,138 --> 00:03:18,926
全套住宅的评分，是各个房间得分，和体形系数的加权。
Its score is a weighted sum of the rooms' scores and its shape factor.

37
00:03:19,376 --> 00:03:21,525
这是当年分数最高的几个结果。
These are some of the highest-scoring results from back then.

38
00:03:25,025 --> 00:03:31,424
把平面组件进行三维建模，就会产生三维预览图。以现在的工具，非常容易。
Model the plan's components in three dimensions and you get a 3D preview. With today's tools, that is very easy.

39
00:03:31,874 --> 00:03:34,904
作为一个试验，它初步实现了生成的能力。
As an experiment, it has achieved a first working ability to generate.

40
00:03:39,004 --> 00:03:43,985
当年，这些步骤分散在几个脚本里，评分的系数要到代码里去改。
Back then these steps were spread over several scripts, and the scoring coefficients had to be changed inside the code.

41
00:03:44,435 --> 00:03:48,197
现在，前端开发成本很低，我把它们收进一个网页：
Today front-end development is cheap, so I gathered them into a single web page:

42
00:03:48,197 --> 00:03:53,758
画样本，看拼图库，改参数，生成房间，组合户型，都在同一个界面里完成。
draw samples, inspect the tile library, set parameters, generate rooms, combine apartments — all in one interface.

43
00:03:53,758 --> 00:03:57,193
对它继续调试的直观性和效率，可以大大提高。
Tuning it further becomes far more intuitive and efficient.

44
00:04:00,493 --> 00:04:06,184
当年我睡在书房里，看着白板，苦心孤诣，花了两个月的业余时间搞这个。
Back then I slept in my study, staring at the whiteboard, and spent two months of spare time working this out.

45
00:04:06,634 --> 00:04:10,734
而且，我一直知道，这里面有过多可以改进的技术。
And I have always known that a great deal in it could be improved technically.

46
00:04:11,184 --> 00:04:14,498
不过，我认为这个方法对于户型的理解非常本质，
Still, I think this method gets at something essential about apartment layouts.

47
00:04:14,498 --> 00:04:18,264
希望它能帮助有兴趣的同学们，增进对这类问题的理解。
I hope it helps interested students understand this kind of problem better.

48
00:04:18,264 --> 00:04:20,825
在这个层面上，它还是具有一些潜力。
At that level, it still has some potential.
